 "title": "Rotary encoder disc in Gray code",
 "width": 500,
 "height": 510,
 "intro": "A disc cut into 8 sectors and 3 rings. Reading clockwise from the top, the sectors are coded 000, 001, 011, 010, 110, 111, 101, 100. At every boundary between neighbouring sectors only one ring changes between clear and shaded, so a sensor sitting on a boundary can misread at most one bit and is never more than one position wrong.",
